a little different with the girls.

241
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:18,784
It's gonna be a lot harder
to get close to them, don't you think?

242
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:20,494
Could be scary for you.

243
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:22,830
I mean, we won't be able
to help you from our room.

244
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,999
- That's true.
- We're separate?

245
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,126
There are always separate bedrooms
for the girls and guys.

246
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:28,294
I have to be with them.

247
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:31,255
Honestly, just imagining it
gives me chills, dude.

248
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,381
Yeah.

249
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:36,844
As a hostess,
I bet she's really good with words.

250
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,387
Like she can butter you up.

251
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:41,682
She knows how to say just
the right thing to get you to like her.

252
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:45,269
She must be talking to Ryopi a lot
since they already know each other.

253
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:46,896
Fine. If they want to talk, let them talk.

254
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,065
Hello, ladies.

255
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:50,900
- Oh, you scared me!
- Hello.

256
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,568
Come in! Oh wait…

257
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:55,529
<i>Kazuma is such a nice guy.</i>
<i>Just look at that smile!</i>

258
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:57,990
- Oh, geez.
- No, it's just, all of you should've come.

259
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:01,661
All right, what's… what's going on
in here, ladies? Talk to me.

260
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:04,497
- Like, what's the vibe in here?
- Deadly.

261
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,248
Deadly?

262
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,917
- She's freaky!
- Deadly.

263
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,919
- Someone's gonna die.
- Deadly is crazy.

264
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:11,045
She's out for blood.

265
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:13,589
What did you tell the other guys
when you came here?

266
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,383
That I was going to the bathroom.

267
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:17,677
- For real?
- And how did they react to that?

268
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:21,347
Actually, I didn't even say that.
I just quietly slipped out, like this.

269
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,685
Sara, you had a lot to say earlier.

270
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,603
Like, "Is this a joke or what?"

271
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:31,232
Well, yeah, a hostess girl,
someone that famous just showing up here--

272
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:34,110
- She can't be looking for love.
- Feels like a publicity stunt.

273
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:35,861
- Is she that famous?
- She's super famous.

274
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,488
- She's a celebrity.
- You never heard of her?

275
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:38,739
- No.
- That explains it!

276
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:41,659
- You don't know her?
- No. Does everyone know her but me?

277
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:44,745
A celebrity hostess
just showed up out of nowhere?

278
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,581
- So, what's the vibe like over there?
- They look like they're having fun?

279
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,834
Just normal. They're just chatting.

280
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:53,504
She doesn't know much about this place,
like when we first got here, so…

281
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,214
Wait, who's, like, excited?

282
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:58,259
Excited? Geez, I dunno.
I wouldn't say they're excited, but…

283
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:00,094
Maru is talking to her a lot.

284
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:01,262
What?

285
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:03,806
I knew it'd be Maru!
We totally called it in here.

286
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:06,517
Wait, really? You called like…
who would talk to her?

287
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,145
We said that it would be Maru or Rune.

288
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:13,899
Well, we're a little afraid that…
I mean, when we're all together…

289
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,278
things will be fine,
but when it's time to go to sleep

290
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:19,572
- and you all go to the girls' room…
- You're worried?

291
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,741
Just wondering what the vibe will be.

292
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:23,576
So you're looking out for everyone.

293
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,619
- For all of us girls. Is that it?
- That's so sweet.

294
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:28,205
- Seriously, you're really sweet.
- I'm not "worried" really.

295
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:31,250
It's more like… I'm just curious
how it's gonna go in your room.

296
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,085
If it'll be a good atmosphere.

297
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,046
Right.

298
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:40,134
Well guys, I have to say,
this is interesting.

299
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:41,302
So, hang on actually,

300
00:12:41,385 --> 00:12:43,429
- I watched Season one…
- Thank you for watching.

301
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:46,348
- Remember when Amo showed up?
- Yikes. Amo. Yep.

302
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:49,685
This situation feels
even more tense than that dynamic.

303
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:50,978
Exactly! Oh my god, no question.

304
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:52,730
This goes way beyond
"Not the damn water" now.

305
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:53,939
This is next level.

306
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:56,066
She threw it.
I guess these ladies are just…

307
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,402
- They like throwing water around.
- They're drawn to it somehow.

308
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,279
<i>Call it a form of self-expression.</i>

309
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:03,449
Right, it's very cathartic. You get upset
and then, bam! Just like that.

310
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:05,576
They're either, throwing,
slamming or making a scene.

311
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:08,996
So true. And my god,
that look on Rinrin's face…

312
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:10,289
She's an open book.

313
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:13,083
I haven't made a face like that in 15--
Actually no, in 20 years.

314
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,960
You don't show that face in public.

315
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,713
But Mimi did talk back a little, right?

316
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,340
She was like, "Shut up, ugly."

317
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:20,966
How do most men…

318
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,802
feel when they see something like that?

319
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:26,055
Well, some of these guys
have a bad-boy kind of past,

320
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:28,140
so they might be more attracted to girls

321
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:31,101
who look like they can take the lead
and fight for what they want.

322
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:33,646
And the other guys might fall
for the vulnerable ones.

323
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:35,523
- We have two types.
- Oh, we just have those two?

324
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:37,191
- I think so.
- Just two?

325
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:40,402
There's pretty much just two.
Especially with these badass boys around.

326
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,445
I see, okay.

327
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,030
So, having said all that, uh…

328
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:44,865
<i>Kazuma was being considerate</i>

329
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:48,786
<i>and went over to the kitchen</i>
<i>for a few minutes to check on the women.</i>

330
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:51,580
But the other four guys
might actually prefer a woman

331
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,750
who's a little more brash
and willing to stir up some trouble.

332
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,044
Where did Kazuma go?

333
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,587
- No idea.
- The bathroom?

334
00:13:58,671 --> 00:13:59,505
- Really?
- Right.

335
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,924
Or he poked his head into the…

336
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,425
The kitchen?

337
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,344
Oh, right. They're cooking.

338
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:08,097
So it's the girls' turn tonight.

339
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,683
- Wait, did you guys cook, too?
- Yesterday.

340
00:14:10,766 --> 00:14:12,184
Really? What did you make? I'm curious.

341
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,353
Maru made burgers,
stewed burgers or something.

342
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:15,688
Wow! Amazing.

343
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:17,106
- It's my specialty.
- Nice!

344
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:19,650
That's some bullshit.

345
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,443
What was that stuff you made, Tai-chan?

346
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:23,153
- What did you make, Tai-chan?
<i>- Bulgogi.</i>

347
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:24,572
<i>Bulgogi? </i>Delicious!

348
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,449
- Ryopi?
- I made fried rice.

349
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,410
So those three dishes?

350
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:31,287
Wait, Kazuma made <i>tonjiru.</i>

351
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,454
Wow, so much variety.

352
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:33,956
But it all came together.

353
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:37,334
Each of us made something,
and then we all came together.

354
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,669
Before that we…

355
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,088
had a little talk
between the men and women.

356
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:44,174
And then,
the men kind of cooked as an apology.

357
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,342
We felt bad.

358
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,511
- Yeah. Mmm-hmm.
- You did something wrong?

359
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:49,138
Well, we sort of…

360
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:51,932
No, it was more like
we just weren't doing enough.

361
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,767
Like, you weren't trying?

362
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:56,145
Actually, I definitely
got chewed out the most.

363
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:57,855
They were like,
"Why aren't you talking more?"

364
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,523
So yeah, they really singled me out.

365
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:02,151
Really? That's weird.
You seem like such a talker.

366
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:03,736
- As of today.
- That's 'cause a girl

367
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:06,739
who's my type showed up today.
So I gotta lay on the charm.

368
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:10,784
Is he running for office?
The guy's making speeches now.

369
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:13,829
- Super subtle t-shirt, too. "Sex"!
- Right, I noticed that too.

370
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:17,207
I'm dying to know
what they're talking about.

371
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,919
They're all still hanging out?

372
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,086
Wait, who?

373
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:22,504
All the guys.

374
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:25,674
Yeah, I guess so.
They're probably still talking.

375
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:28,260
Two, four, six. Hmm…

376
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,554
- Nine. There's more over here.
- We're short.

377
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:31,597
Oh, okay, good.

378
00:15:32,973 --> 00:15:34,350
Ooh, nice, looks delicious!

379
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:36,352
<i>Man, they really went all out.</i>

380
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:38,228
<i>What if some if it</i>
<i>is secretly spicy as hell?</i>

381
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,438
Do we carry these?

382
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:41,523
- How do we move them?
- Good question.

383
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,442
I'm the representative director.

384
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:45,319
- Oh, wow.
- So I do both.

385
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:47,029
I'm a manager and a host.

386
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,155
- Mmm…
- Yep.

387
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:50,616
- How long you been doing that?
- About two years.

388
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:53,035
- Oh, okay.
- I've been with the club for ten years.

389
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,912
- The whole time.
- Impressive. He worked his way up.

390
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:56,455
Ten years is amazing.

391
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:57,957
- I'm loyal to them.
- Oh, here they are.

392
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,959
- Can you help carry stuff?
- Here they come.

393
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:03,462
- Here we go.
- Oh, are we bringing the food in here?

394
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:06,382
Yeah, we'll just go grab the food
from the kitchen and bring it here.

395
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:08,509
- Is this trash?
- Ah, no… I mean, yeah.

396
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,719
Man, my heart is pounding right now.

397
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:12,179
- I'm on edge, yikes.
- Yeesh.

398
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:13,305
Little scary.

399
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,558
- Something smells so good.
- Smells damn good.

400
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,103
- It really does.
- Guess what we made?

401
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,688
It smells incredible.

402
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:24,400
- Get ready for a feast, boys.
- That looks so good. Oh, man.

403
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:27,027
- What can I carry?
- Do we have spoons and stuff? Silverware?

404
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:29,613
- Oh, yeah, over there.
- Should we take those then?

405
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:34,868
- Like this?
- Mmm.

406
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:36,912
- I can take another bowl.
- One too many?

407
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:39,915
Oh, no, this one should go here.

408
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:42,209
Yeah, I lost count.
Soup goes on the right, doesn't it?

409
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:44,086
Let's put that here…

410
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,714
and this there.

411
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:49,550
Whoa, shoot.

412
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:52,011
Rune has been counting this whole time…

413
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,554
This one could fall.

414
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,890
One, two…

415
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,642
All right, that's good.

416
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,436
It's wet here for some reason.

417
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:04,314
- There we go.
- We need one more.

418
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:08,110
- Huh? One, two, three, four…
- I think like four people

419
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:10,112
- will probably sit on that side.
- Ah, yeah, I got you.

420
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:11,238
One, two, three, four…

421
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,450
It's fine, it's fine.
Let's just leave them like this for now.

422
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:16,744
But this is how they should be, right?

423
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,996
- I want a full plate.
- Looks nice.

424
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:21,540
- I want a small plate.
- This might be too much.

425
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:22,750
Do we have chopsticks?

426
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:24,752
We do. Wait. We're missing one pair.

427
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:25,878
Here you go.

428
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:27,713
- Thank you.
- One pair.

429
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:29,757
So, where did my food go?

430
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,134
Yeah, we're definitely one short.

431
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:34,803
- What! Okay. Eat mine.
- No, I'm good, really.

432
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,598
Nine portions?

433
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:38,515
Where's mine?

434
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:40,934
<i>What the?</i>

435
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,187
How many did you guys make?

436
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,146
Nine.

437
00:17:44,229 --> 00:17:46,315
- <i>Are they serious?</i>
<i>- </i>Nine portions?

438
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,984
Whoa, whoa, what is this?
Some prison hazing tactic?

439
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:53,822
It's like they're trying to intimidate
the new guy in the cellblock.

440
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,574
It's getting a little spooky.

441
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:56,784
Let's divvy some up.

442
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:59,328
Oh, no, it's okay. I can go make some.

443
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:01,455
- No, it's okay.
- Seriously, just eat. Go ahead.

444
00:18:01,538 --> 00:18:02,414
Where's mine?

445
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:06,752
- How much did you make?
- Not enough.

446
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:08,587
There's no more left in the kitchen.

447
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,256
Is there any rice left?

448
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,883
- Uh, yeah.
- There is?

449
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:15,844
- Oh, no, Tai-chan, I'm sorry!
- No problem.

450
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,930
- Come on, let's make some.
- Go ahead and start eating.

451
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:20,390
- I can't eat that much anyway.
- Let's cook.

452
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,810
- No worries. Let's hit the kitchen.
- No, seriously, I feel so bad.

453
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:24,478
Don't even worry about it.

454
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:27,523
I mean, how can they
be missing exactly one serving?

455
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,109
Honestly, just forget about it.

456
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,985
Oh, this is enough for me.
There's some here.

457
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:32,903
What about rice?

458
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,905
No, I'm good.

459
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:36,824
We're definitely one short.

460
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:37,950
They screwed up?

461
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:41,411
Well, we have some left.
There's still a little bit here.

462
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,913
Let's bring this over there.

463
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:45,040
Wait, what about rice?
You're gonna eat rice, right?

464
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,291
We still have rice too, right?

465
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:48,127
- Yeah.
- Then this is good.

466
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:50,754
Seriously, nothing to worry about.

467
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,798
- This is for you, Rune?
- Yeah.

468
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,508
Okay. How much do you want?

469
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:56,218
- Just a normal portion.
- For real. I'm okay.

470
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:57,261
Just need a few bites.

471
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,721
- There's plenty here for me.
- You can give her a smaller plate.

472
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,640
- Uh, here.
- Thanks. Sorry about that.

473
00:19:23,036 --> 00:19:24,663
These look delicious.

474
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:33,463
Was this a mistake?

475
00:19:35,757 --> 00:19:37,426
That there wasn't enough food.

476
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,511
No, it wasn't a mistake.

477
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:40,804
So you didn't make enough?

478
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,557
We just didn't dish it up.

479
