00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:51,910
So anyone could end up being
either the victim or the bully

725
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:53,328
depending on the situation.

726
00:31:53,411 --> 00:31:54,954
But when problems like that come up,

727
00:31:55,038 --> 00:31:56,998
it almost turns into
an <i>After School Special.</i>

728
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:59,459
It's a reality dating show. Don't forget.
It's not educational.

729
00:31:59,542 --> 00:32:00,919
- It's not family drama?
- A mega-family.

730
00:32:01,002 --> 00:32:03,588
I can tell you're struggling with this.
It's a reality dating show, guys.

731
00:32:03,671 --> 00:32:05,965
We really saw them realize
that the dynamic can change on a dime.

732
00:32:06,049 --> 00:32:07,508
Oh, yeah, that's interesting.

733
00:32:07,592 --> 00:32:09,385
I think that's so important
for a group like this.

734
00:32:09,469 --> 00:32:10,303
Oh, for sure.

735
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:13,181
You're right, and Rune said it
straight out, that was actually…

736
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:15,266
That was great. He's a real role model.

737
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:16,184
Definitely.

738
00:32:16,267 --> 00:32:19,020
- What a guy. He's a model prisoner.
- A model prisoner!

739
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:20,939
Taka, he's not a prisoner.

740
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:22,774
No, listen.
This is a heartfelt family drama.

741
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:24,734
- It's not a family drama either, guys.
- Are you sure?

742
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:26,361
- Slow down.
- Rune is the overworked dad.

743
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:28,655
No, they're not all Rune's kids.

744
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,116
- Morning.
- Good morning.

745
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:33,326
Let's go smoke.

746
00:32:34,118 --> 00:32:35,119
So how is it?

747
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,079
What do you mean?

748
00:32:36,579 --> 00:32:39,374
Like, how do you feel?
Now that we've got a new transfer student.

749
00:32:39,457 --> 00:32:42,543
No, wait, I wanna hear
what it's like for you right now.

750
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:45,755
It's been a whirlwind.
Way more than I expected.

751
00:32:45,838 --> 00:32:49,008
I mean, in terms of how things
have developed since we got here.

752
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:50,802
I haven't been able to process all of it.

753
00:32:50,885 --> 00:32:52,303
But to be honest…

754
00:32:53,429 --> 00:32:54,931
I don't think my feelings have changed.

755
00:32:55,014 --> 00:32:56,057
Oh, really?

756
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:59,185
That's interesting,
'cause to shoot straight with you,

757
00:32:59,268 --> 00:33:01,688
I thought she seemed like your type.
I mean…

758
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:02,855
The transfer student.

759
00:33:02,939 --> 00:33:03,982
- Interesting.
- Yeah.

760
00:33:04,065 --> 00:33:05,817
"Shoot straight with you?"

761
00:33:05,900 --> 00:33:08,111
Is she in a western or something?

762
00:33:08,194 --> 00:33:10,029
I feel like mostly old men say that.

763
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:12,573
- Or Dirty Harry.
- That's a weird way to put it.

764
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:14,242
- She seems like my type?
- Yeah.

765
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:15,159
Okay.

766
00:33:15,243 --> 00:33:19,664
Um, I was really starting to feel unsure
about the whole thing actually.

767
00:33:19,747 --> 00:33:21,082
- Hmm.
- Yeah.

768
00:33:21,165 --> 00:33:23,543
What do you mean by "unsure"?
I'm dying to know.

769
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:25,294
No, like, just-- Like, um…

770
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:27,005
I guess I…

771
00:33:27,088 --> 00:33:28,464
I wasn't exactly jealous,

772
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:30,299
but maybe I was feeling
something close to that,

773
00:33:30,383 --> 00:33:31,759
just to shoot straight with you.

774
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,094
<i>She said it again.</i>

775
00:33:33,177 --> 00:33:34,470
Mmm, so, like,

776
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:37,390
that's why it was hard for me
to talk to you this way.

777
00:33:37,473 --> 00:33:40,268
And when you asked me
to come out and smoke before,

778
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:42,812
my first thought was "eh, I don't know"
but yeah, I decided to come.

779
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:44,939
"I don't know" sounds bad to me.

780
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:46,190
Isn't that a bad sign?

781
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:48,568
Um, yeah, I just wasn't sure
if I'd be able to talk to you.

782
00:33:48,651 --> 00:33:49,652
- Why?
- I was worried

783
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:53,448
that nothing I said would come out right
because of those jealous feelings.

784
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:56,826
That's why I was like,
"I don't know. It could be tough." Yeah.

785
00:33:56,909 --> 00:33:58,661
- No, I get it.
- Mmm.

786
00:34:02,582 --> 00:34:05,960
- Kazuma, let's go for a smoke.
- Oh, sure.

787
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,211
I mean, like…

788
00:34:07,962 --> 00:34:09,380
Until now…

789
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:11,632
he hasn't really taken the lead, you know?

790
00:34:12,216 --> 00:34:14,927
But he did in that situation.
I thought it was gross.

791
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:17,805
You mean, the whole thing with Mimi?
I got you.

792
00:34:19,640 --> 00:34:21,893
Like, I get
that it's because they're friends.

793
00:34:21,976 --> 00:34:23,144
Mmm-hmm.

794
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:27,774
I was interested in him,
he was, like, top choice for me.

795
00:34:28,608 --> 00:34:29,692
But now he's…

796
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:32,904
- way down the list.
- He fell that far?

797
00:34:32,987 --> 00:34:34,614
Yeah, I'm so much less interested in him.

798
00:34:34,697 --> 00:34:36,657
- You're really pulling away from him, huh?
- It's crazy.

799
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:37,825
It happened so fast.

800
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:44,165
He's had you on his mind
the whole time, though.

801
00:34:44,248 --> 00:34:45,166
- For real.
- Really?

802
00:34:45,249 --> 00:34:48,461
Yeah. He kept saying, "Man, I need to talk
to Rinrin," like non-stop.

803
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:49,420
He did?

804
00:34:52,048 --> 00:34:55,093
So why don't you try
talking to him, just once?

805
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,427
Hmm…

806
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:58,805
But you won't know
how he feels if you don't talk to him.

807
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:00,932
Then things are just gonna
stay like this with you guys.

808
00:35:01,015 --> 00:35:02,016
Sure, you're right, but…

809
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:04,227
I think it'd be
a good idea to talk to him.

810
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:07,730
I don't know. I don't
really want to talk to him right now.

811
00:35:09,232 --> 00:35:10,733
I feel like talking to him--

812
00:35:10,817 --> 00:35:14,112
It makes me feel uncomfortable too,
when we still have, you know,

813
00:35:14,195 --> 00:35:16,239
all this time together ahead of us here.

814
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:17,281
Yeah, you're right.

815
00:35:17,865 --> 00:35:19,659
I don't think I'll approach him.

816
00:35:19,742 --> 00:35:21,869
If he comes to me, I'll think about it.

817
00:35:27,291 --> 00:35:28,292
Rinrin, can I talk to you?

818
00:35:28,376 --> 00:35:30,253
- <i>Oh, right on cue!</i>
- <i>He came!</i>

819
00:35:30,336 --> 00:35:31,379
That cool, Kazuma?

820
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:32,421
Of course.

821
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:34,423
<i>Wow! Kazuma is such a nice guy!</i>

822
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:36,384
<i>Man, I really like Kazuma.</i>

823
00:35:36,467 --> 00:35:38,010
Thank you. Sorry.

824
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:42,515
So, Rinrin.

825
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:45,935
- Yeah, what?
- What're you mad about?

826
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:48,271
Was it how I escorted her?

827
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:49,772
I don't know if "escort" is the word.

828
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:52,066
Or was it the time
I invited her to sit down?

829
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:55,945
I'm trying to shoot straight with you,
I don't know why you're mad.

830
00:35:56,028 --> 00:35:58,781
- "Shoot straight." You gotta be kidding.
- Is this some kind of prison slang?

831
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:00,741
Still don't think they're prisoners.

832
00:36:00,825 --> 00:36:03,202
Look, from where I'm sitting,
the thing is…

833
00:36:04,078 --> 00:36:06,330
When I told her that she should sit down,

834
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:09,542
I wasn't, you know, trying to make
a move on her or anything.

835
00:36:09,625 --> 00:36:11,043
Like that wasn't it at all.

836
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:12,253
I mean I was just…

837
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:15,965
caught off guard
because a friend of mine showed up.

838
00:36:16,048 --> 00:36:18,926
Um… how do I put this?
So what if she's your friend, dude?

839
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:23,181
I seriously couldn't care less.

840
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:24,307
Okay, fair enough.

841
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:27,935
Like, so what? You know?

842
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:32,356
Because, the fact is,
up until she came here,

843
00:36:32,940 --> 00:36:35,401
you haven't really
been taking the lead at all.

844
00:36:35,484 --> 00:36:38,738
But then suddenly you do it right away
when she's around. And I'm like, "wow."

845
00:36:39,739 --> 00:36:40,781
It's kind of gross.

846
00:36:44,660 --> 00:36:47,038
<i>Guys like him</i>
<i>probably hate this kind of thing.</i>

847
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:47,955
<i>Hmm.</i>

848
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:49,999
<i>He's thinking,</i>
<i>"Oh, this girl's a handful."</i>

849
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:52,001
But, that was just me,

850
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:52,919
um…

851
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:54,754
kind of…

852
00:36:56,088 --> 00:36:59,175
I think I would've done the same thing
no matter who came.

853
00:36:59,258 --> 00:37:01,177
I knew everyone
would give her the cold shoulder

854
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,970
'cause she's a transfer student.

855
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:07,266
And I thought it was a little rude
to make her stand there for so long.

856
00:37:07,350 --> 00:37:09,977
So, since the seat next to me was open,
I told her to sit down.

857
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:11,229
That's just polite.

858
00:37:24,825 --> 00:37:26,494
Well, I wanted to come out here

859
00:37:26,577 --> 00:37:30,456
so I could apologize for making you
feel that way. I hope you understand.

860
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:34,460
I'm really sorry.

861
00:37:36,128 --> 00:37:37,171
Hmm. Okay.

862
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:38,798
Sorry.

863
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:40,466
Thank you.

864
00:37:41,676 --> 00:37:42,551
See you tomorrow.

865
00:37:42,635 --> 00:37:43,803
Mmm-hmm.

866
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:44,720
Good night.

867
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:45,763
Good night.

868
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:08,160
Ooh, the plot thickens.

869
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:10,746
So true, so true.
I'm gonna shoot straight about--

870
00:38:10,830 --> 00:38:12,707
Oh, man. Here we go, cowboy!

871
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:14,834
- Are we making this a thing?
- A hundred percent.

872
00:38:14,917 --> 00:38:16,377
It's our official phrase.

873
00:38:16,460 --> 00:38:19,463
Let's talk about the conversation
between Ryopi and Rinrin.

874
00:38:19,547 --> 00:38:21,173
If I were in Rune's position,

875
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:22,883
I'd prefer it if she just
came out and said,

876
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:25,511
"I didn't like that you did that".
No attitude, just calm…

877
00:38:25,594 --> 00:38:27,054
I might even feel flattered by that.

878
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:29,140
There's a chance that would
tug on your heartstrings.

879
00:38:29,223 --> 00:38:32,643
I think all she needed to do
was let him know as clearly as she could

880
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:35,313
that she's been
focused on him this whole time.

881
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:36,397
That makes sense.

882
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:40,234
But remember, guys, Rinrin has been
cheated on like six times so far.

883
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:41,444
Oh, so she has trauma.

884
00:38:41,527 --> 00:38:43,696
So naturally she might be
a little more sensitive

885
00:38:43,779 --> 00:38:45,197
about that than most people.

886
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:47,199
What Ryopi did
doesn't count as cheating, right?

887
00:38:47,283 --> 00:38:49,535
I guess she can't help imagining
the worst-case scenario

888
00:38:49,618 --> 00:38:51,162
of where that could lead.

889
00:38:51,245 --> 00:38:53,706
Let's pick which guy
Mimi should fall in love with

890
00:38:53,789 --> 00:38:55,291
so that everything works out for the best.

891
00:38:55,374 --> 00:38:56,375
Oh, yeah! Perfect!

892
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:58,961
- That's one way to resolve this.
- Let's see.

893
00:38:59,045 --> 00:39:00,546
Who would be a good target?

894
00:39:00,629 --> 00:39:02,673
It's not gonna be Maru, right?

895
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:05,051
- Right.
- Ayacheru would be crushed.

896
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:06,927
Kazuma.

897
00:39:07,011 --> 00:39:07,845
Kazuma!

898
00:39:07,928 --> 00:39:10,139
It's gotta be him. He's the best bet.

899
00:39:10,222 --> 00:39:11,599
Quite messing around!

900
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:13,392
You can't say Kazuma, okay?

901
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:14,602
You're the producer!
